WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:02.890
How far out are we going?

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.400
Do you know where the Number is located?

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.320
Yes. I saw it in the depth of your memory.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.550
In my memory? What do you mean by that?

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.210
All you need do is keep quiet and follow my instructions.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.730
But before we retrieve the Number, we have to search for him.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:23.790
Him?

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.850
The Different Dimension Airship is showing us the location for the second Number.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.130
Wow!

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.680
So our next destination is
 some ancient ruins in a deserted island?

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.610
What traps await us this time?

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.540
There might be a Barian there again.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.840
Hmph! Fine by me!

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.810
Go forth, Yuma Mach Bringin' It!

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:46.730
Yuma Mach?

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.060
When did we start calling it that?

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:50.310
It's fine, ain't it?!

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.740
He's got absolutely no naming sense.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.350
Senator Parker!

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.580
Senator Parker!

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.330
Thank you so much!

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:03.850
Senator Parker!

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.040
Senator Parker!

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.710
We are sincerely grateful to you for traveling all the way here to donate so much money

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.500
to the Children's Library Foundation.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.820
It is nothing to be praised for.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.270
Children are the treasure of the world.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.680
And he just donated to the
 Children's Center Corporation a few days ago!

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.900
Senator Parker's really a good man!

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.770
He's always lending a hand to those in need of help!

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.300
He's always thinking about the citzens' needs first and foremost!

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.320
Boss, this is last night's earnings.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.750
And we'll ambush those guys at the harbor tonight.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.090
You understand, don't you?

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:49.370
Not a single one of the guys you jump is to crawl back here alive.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.340
Okay, Boss...

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:01.520
Now I see. On the outside, you appear as an enthusiastic and highly charitable politician.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.960
But on the inside, you're a two-faced smuggler.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.930
An underworld boss who'll do anything to get what he wants.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.050
Admirable double-dealing there.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.520
Who the hell are you?!

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.140
I'm hoping you'll stop the lazy 
acting and show your true form already.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.840
If I recall, you were with together with Yuma Tuskumo.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.260
And who are you? You don't seem to be some regular human.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.930
I've been searching for you, Number 96.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.850
I am Vector of the Seven Barian Emperors.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.890
I would like to become your subordinate.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.020
This guy's a real piece of work!

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:53.710
A Barian like <i>you</i>... as my underling?!

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.180
I believe that you are the true king.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.350
I can grant you massive power.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.490
What is your goal?

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:07.490
It's only natural for those with power to join forces when they have common interests.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.460
And you think you and I share common interests?

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:15.960
You don't seem to have any intention
 of trying to save the Astral World.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.460
But I have no intention of saving the Barian World either.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:22.550
What if I told you I was thinking the same thing?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.550
Oh...?

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:29.100
To prove my loyalty, I will tell you
 where you can find a new Number.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.690
A new Number?

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.900
Doesn't sound like a bad plan, now does it?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.280
A Barian Rank-Up Magic Card?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.610
So you're handing me the power of Barian?

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.160
A true king must be unmatched.

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.370
Very well. I'll hear what you have to say.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.180
I thought I'd borrow this man's body

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:00.510
in order to observe the human world,
 but I've grown bored of that.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.970
Let's go, my servant!

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:42.690
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.740
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:53.200
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:56.750
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.630
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:07.970
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.180
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.060
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:18.690
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.770
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:30.240
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.200
Whoa, whoa! Ow, ow!

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.950
"The Cunning Vector - Astral vs. Number 96"

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.280
Yuma, take your seat already!

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.950
Things are pretty rough outside.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.370
It would seem that the range of space
 within the Different Dimensions

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.460
has caused a distortion in space.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.880
God. This bastard never quits.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.760
This phenomenon occurring within the Different Dimensions

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.720
has the same presence I felt before.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.060
Just what is it...?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.280
So the new Number is here.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.990
<i>What the hell is this horrible feeling?!</i>

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.660
<i>As if every hair on my body's started standing up!</i>

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:38.620
<i>What are you laughing at?!</i>

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.170
<i>So you really can feel it, huh?</i>

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.630
What the hell did you do?!

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.340
It isn't necessary for you to know now.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:48.930
What?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:54.760
Anyway, if you absorb this Number 96 inside yourself,

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.470
you'll have use for it.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.310
<i>I know that...! I'm waiting for the right opportunity!</i>

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:00.940
What is it?

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.860
No, it's nothing.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.120
What an unsettling presence.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:19.710
I can hear the screams of human spirits crossing all times crying out their malice!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.120
Malice...?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:27.130
Humans are creatures who build history atop endless piles of resentment and hypocrisy.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.130
How foolish they are.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.470
Now then, where shall we go next?

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:45.480
Oh? It's like you've been here before.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:46.900
No...

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.240
My body moved on its own...

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.580
Wow! So these are the ruins where the Number's located?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.300
Is this the entrance?

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.220
This place... might be very dangerous...

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.220
D-Dangerous?!

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.100
If possible, I'd like it if we didn't enter.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.600
But the map points us here.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:24.850
I...guess that's true.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.530
It's pretty creepy here...

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.070
This wall...

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.530
Is this the legend of these ruins?

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.910
There's grief gathered here...

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.290
From people of the past.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.420
P-People of the past?

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.210
S-Stop that... It's kinda scary!

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.880
It's life energy crossing over time itself.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.880
That's what the walls speak of.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.220
The legend of the cursed royal palace.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.520
A prince who governed this island
 used to dwell inside this royal palace.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:07.060
He was childish and had no faith in humanity.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.440
He doubted everyone and anyone, casting judgment upon them.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.860
He lived as a person who stole the lives from everyone around him,

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:20.530
and as the last standing, the prince severed his own life as well.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.370
The cursed legend...

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.210
Rio!

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.130
I'm okay...

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:35.510
<i>The prince governing this island
 stole the lives of everyone, including himself?</i>

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.550
Cursed... royal palace...

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.310
This place is...

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:56.740
This seems to be the plaza where the executions were held.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:00.280
It's a fitting place for taking so many human lives.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:04.040
<i>What is it? This emotion akin to the feeling of fear?</i>

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.130
So you've come, Yuma... Astral...

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.540
So it seems.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:16.380
Then I'll just have to beat them straight down to Hell!

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.390
Screw that! I'm the one who's after Yuma Tsukumo-

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.560
You'll have your share later.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.640
<i>Wh-What did you say?! That...!</i>

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:30.600
But before that, I have to obtain the Number.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.080
This is...

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.630
So you're the one protecting this Number.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:08.270
How amusing. You plan to test to see which of us is stronger?

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:14.940
I'm getting riled with excitement!

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.360
Duel!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.280
Which way are we supposed to go?

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.580
There's a mark on that one, so we should go there!

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:32.960
Wait, Yuma!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.000
Wait! There might be a trap there!

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.340
It's okay! Leave it to me!

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:46.890
What was that just now?

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:52.310
No way!

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.480
Run!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.900
What the heck is that thing?!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.950
I found another mark!

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.460
Made it out by a hair.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.460
Hey, Yuma!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.760
All the paths you choose are filled with traps!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.170
Quite the thrill, ain't it?

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.220
But who put that sign there?

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:26.970
It was probably my dad.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.930
Your dad?

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.890
Yeah, my dad's just like that.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.230
He likes to mark paths that have the least amount of traps.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:36.940
That's pretty impressive.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.020
Wow, you're making me blush!

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.150
She wasn't complimenting <i>you</i>, you know.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.080
What's going on here?!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.800
Ouch!

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:01.010
Yuma.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:01.800
Where are we?

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.130
Wh-What the? A jail house?

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:06.550
Hey, Yuma!

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:07.340
Yuma!

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.970
Guys! You all okay?!

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:10.760
Yeah!

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:12.890
Where are we?

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.270
We seem to have fallen into a trap/

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.820
Yo there! It's been a long time!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.030
Dear Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.610
Y-You're Vector!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.860
C'mon, that's mean!

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.280
You're not gonna call me Shingetsu anymore, Yuma-<i>kun</i>?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.410
You jerk!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.410
I've got some bad news for you after you came all this way.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.540
The Number's already been taken!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:38.540
What?!

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.380
Well, since you came all this way, I'll leave you with a good taste in your mouth.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:45.050
How 'bout it? Feel like Dueling with the Number at stake?

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.590
Fine by me! I'll take you on!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:55.230
Well then, Yuma, we'll need you to switch over to your special <i>deluxe suite</i>.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:00.980
Yuma!

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.150
The heck is this?

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:12.370
If you don't deactivate the <i>special equipment</i> on that spot

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.490
you won't get out!

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.830
I got all sorts of new information on the Number here from the machinery around this place!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.790
From this Labyrinth of Screams set up here!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:26.260
Screw that! I can't Duel you from a place like this!

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:30.050
Calm <i>down</i>. <i>You</i> won't be the one Dueling.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.720
Astral will!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:33.850
Astra will?!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.810
You must be planning something
 with bad intentions for the worst!

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:40.520
Whoa there! That's my personal catchphrase!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:41.440
Very well.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:43.570
Astral!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.990
I will accept this Duel. Come down here.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:53.450
Too bad, but your opponent won't be <i>me</i>, Astral.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:58.330
Him?!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.830
Number 96!

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.170
It's been a while, Astral.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.800
In here, we can Duel each other to our heart's content.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.510
The Number is right <i>here</i>.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:12.550
That card...! Don't tell me you've teamed up with the Barians?!

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:17.600
The enemy just decided to lend me a hand of their own will, so I'm being nice and giving them a hand.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:22.940
I did promise that I'd come take your body one of these days.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.520
The time's come to realize that!

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.190
Once I defeat you in a Duel, that is!

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.740
Duel Disk, set!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.330
Yuma, I'm borrowing your cards!

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.370
Go for it!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.800
I'm going to make you realize!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:53.890
That I'm far different from the last time we fought!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.180
Duel!!

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.430
My turn! Draw!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.270
I Summon Malicevorous Spoon!

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:10.690
Then, by sending Malicevorous Knife from my hand to the Graveyard,

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:13.030
I can Special Summon Malicevorous Fork!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:20.120
This guy can be Special Summoned by sending a Malicevorous Monster from my hand to the Graveyard!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:23.790
Then I activate the effect of Malicevorous Spoon!

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:29.130
This guy, once per turn, when a Malicevorous Monster is Special Summoned,

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:33.090
can Special Summon a Level Two or lower Malicevorous Monster from my Graveyard!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.800
Come forth, Malicevorous Knife!

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.680
He already played three Level Two Monsters!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:48.360
I Overlay the Level Two Malicevorous Spoon, Knife, and Fork!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:52.950
I build the Overlay Network using these three Monsters!

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.860
Xyz Summon!

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:59.620
Come forth, my avatar! Number 96!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:04.160
The Envoy of Pitch Black Darkness! Black Mist!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.830
Black Mist?!

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:11.590
During a battle, by detaching one Overlay Unit, Black Mist can

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.880
halve the Attack Power of one of the opponent's Monsters

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:17.970
and increase its own Attack Power by that same amount.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:19.970
In other words, no matter who opposes it,

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:24.390
Black Mist will always be at least 100 points stronger than it.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.600
No one stands a chance against this Monster.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:33.400
I set one card! Turn end!

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.160
My turn! Draw!

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.700
I Special Summon Toy Knight from my hand!

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.450
When I control no Monsters on the field,

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.080
I can Special Summon this Monster from my hand!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.300
I will then Normal Summon another Toy Knight!

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.140
He's got two Level Four Monsters...

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:04.220
Astral! Are you planning to Summon Hope?!

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:09.310
Did you really think I didn't anticipate this strategy?!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:14.610
You Summoned two Toy Knights not to Summon Hope,

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:19.700
but to have your two Toy Knights force Black Mist to use up its Overlay Units!

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:22.660
You planned to use these low Attack Power Monsters

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:26.910
to minimize the amount of damage you take as a result!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:31.250
I activate the Continuous Trap, Small Stopper!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:36.880
This field will prevent all Monsters with 1000 or less Attack Points from attacking!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:43.640
And if a Monster in Attack Position doesn't attack,

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:47.180
you'll receive 1000 points of damage during the end of your turn!

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:50.150
Shoot! Not only has the Toy Knights' attacks been sealed,

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:53.270
but Astral's gonna take 1000 points of damage!

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:57.190
I Overlay the two Level Four Toy Knights!

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:03.280
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:05.240
Xyz Summon!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.040
Come forth, Number 39!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.920
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.630
Hope!

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:22.140
Once his Toy Knights' attacks were sealed,

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.300
he went and Summoned Hope, huh?

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:28.770
Hope won't stand a chance against Black Mist!
 What're you gonna do, Astral?!

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:33.060
Yuma, do you think I Summoned Hope for nothing?

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:35.360
What?

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:39.950
I activate the Equip Magic, Exchange Guard Robe, from my hand!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:45.030
Using this card's effect, Hope's Attack Power increases by 500 points!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.700
I use Aspiring Emperor - Hope to attack Black Mist!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.580
I activate Black Mist's effect!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:56.550
I detach one Overlay Unit to halve the opponent's Monster's Attack Power!

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:00.590
Black Mist will then receive that same amount as its Attack Power!

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.930
Shadow Gain!

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.060
If this continues, Hope's done for!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.150
Too bad for you, Astral!

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.530
Are you sure?

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:19.530
What?

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.570
I use this moment to activate Exchange Guard Robe's other effect!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.070
When the equipped Monster's Attack Power

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:28.410
changes due to an effect other than this card,

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:33.750
the opposing player takes damage equal to the difference in points changed!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.710
Now you'll be taking 1500 points of damage!

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:45.430
I get it. Now he can use Black Mist's effect against him.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.980
Then, by detaching one Overlay Unit from Hope,

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.110
this battle will be negated!

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.990
Heck yeah! He scored a head start punch!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:09.790
I expected no less.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.290
But do you think I took that damage for nothing?

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:14.410
What?

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:17.960
What the?

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:22.920
Yuma!

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.470
What's going on here?!

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.470
Oh <i>yeah</i>! I forgot to <i>mention</i> that!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.890
When Number 96's Life Points decrease,

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:35.440
one of the machines within this Labyrinth of Screams will activate.

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:37.730
Wh-What'd you say?!

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:42.440
Shit!

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.860
Then in this Duel, Astral...!

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:47.160
It means he can't attack.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.200
That's cowardly!

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:51.950
It means the cards I hold in my <i>hand</i>
 aren't <i>just</i> cards from my deck!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:57.370
This Labyrinth of Screams will serve to stop you from making a move in addition to this Continuous Trap!

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:01.420
Now then... What'll you do, Astral?

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:24.110
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:26.650
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:27.860
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:29.280
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:34.660
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:37.210
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:38.290
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:39.330
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:42.710
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:45.050
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:48.170
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.390
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:53.390
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:55.350
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:56.730
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:58.600
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:02.900
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:07.990
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:09.240
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:13.240
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:18.620
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:19.830
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:23.960
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.340
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:43.480
Thanks to Vector's horrible trap,

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:46.570
I've been trapped in a losing Duel against Number 96.

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:50.490
It's become a hostage Duel with Yuma's life on the line.

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.320
Astral, forget about me and kick his ass!

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:55.030
Look out, Yuma!

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:56.950
Isn't there anything I can do?

00:23:56.950 --> 00:23:59.910
You must have realized, Yuma!

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:02.710
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:06.250
"Realm of Chaos: Number 96, the Incarnation of Insanity!!"

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.670
Black Mist's become a Chaos?!
